Q.parties.forEach(function (p) { Q[p + '_in_government'] = 0; });
!}

= The Directory

In the second week of December the Reichstag is adjourned without a date. Seeckt announces a Directory: himself, the Krupp director Otto Wiedfeldt, Kahr from Munich, a banker and a judge of the Reich Court. Ebert signs the decree after the army tells him what will happen if he does not.

The Directory dissolves the Saxon and Thuringian Landtags, puts the unions under a state commissioner, and makes membership of our party punishable by five years in prison. The SPD protests in the press. A week later it is banned in Saxony too.

- @underground: Stay in Germany and go underground.
- @exile: Send the leadership to Prague.

@underground
subtitle: The party becomes a conspiracy for as long as the Directory lasts.
on-arrival: {!
Q.ending_id = 3;
Q.e23_dir_choice = 1;
!}

The Zentrale moves into safe flats and allotment huts. It will meet in daylight again only when the generals have gone.

- @end: See how it ends.

@exile
subtitle: The leaders stay alive. The cells at home are on their own.
on-arrival: {!
Q.ending_id = 3;
Q.e23_dir_choice = 2;
Q.independence -= 10;
!}

The leaders cross into Czechoslovakia at night through the woods of the Erzgebirge. The cells in Germany keep on without them.

- @end: See how it ends.

@end
go-to: game_over
